      "notes": [
        "The article is il- or l-, added to the start of a noun or an adjective. familja is a family. il-familja is the family. kuġin is a cousin. il-kuġin is the cousin.",
        "Before a vowel (a, e, i, ie, o, u), and before għ and h, use l-: l-omm, l-hena, l-għasfur, l-aħwa.",
        "Before a sun consonant, the l changes to that letter: id-dundjan, iċ-ċavetta, in-nanna, ir-raġel, it-tabib, ix-xalpa, iż-żarbun, iz-zokk.",
        "Moon consonants keep il-. Għ and h are moon consonants, but they take l-: il-missier, il-ħabib, l-għajn, l-hena.",
        "The notes write the school as l-iskola, not is-skola.",
        "The i in il- is called il-vokali tal-leħen, the euphonic vowel. It drops before a vowel, għ, or h. It also drops when the word before the article already ends in a vowel: Dan l-orgni li xtrajt. Dan huwa l-pjanist."
      ]
