    {
      "id": "particles",
      "title": "Particles",
      "blurb": "The article, and the small words in the sentences.",
      "kind": "particles",
      "lead": "il- is the article from the class notes, including how it is formed. The other words are small patterns you meet in the sentences.",
      "items": [
        {
          "word": "il-",
          "means": "the",
          "formed": "The article is il- or l-. Before a vowel, and before għ and h, use l-: l-art, l-omm, l-għasfur, l-hena. Before a sun consonant the l changes: iċ-ċavetta, id-dundjan, in-nanna, ir-raġel, is-sodda, it-tabib, ix-xalpa, iż-żarbun, iz-zokk. Before the other consonants, il- stays: il-missier, il-ktieb, il-qalb. The i is il-vokali tal-leħen. It also drops when the word before already ends in a vowel: Dan huwa l-pjanist.",
          "example": "l-omm, il-missier, iċ-ċavetta",
          "gloss": "the mother, the father, the key"
        },
        {
          "word": "ma … x",
          "means": "not",
          "formed": "ma goes before the verb. x joins the end. Nifhem becomes Ma nifhimx. Before a vowel or għ, ma is often written m': M'għandix.",
          "example": "Ma nifhimx.",
          "gloss": "I do not understand."
        },
        {
          "word": "li",
          "means": "that, who, which",
          "formed": "li does not change. It starts the clause that follows.",
          "example": "Naf li inti hawn.",
          "gloss": "I know that you are here."
        },
        {
          "word": "biex",
          "means": "in order to",
          "formed": "biex does not change. A verb in the present follows it.",
          "example": "Ġejt biex nitgħallem.",
          "gloss": "I came in order to learn."
        },
        {
          "word": "qed",
          "means": "happening now",
          "formed": "qed does not change. The longer form agrees: qiegħed for he, qiegħda for she, qegħdin for they.",
          "example": "Qed niekol.",
          "gloss": "I am eating."
        },
        {
          "word": "se",
          "means": "going to",
          "formed": "se does not take an ending. ħa and ser do the same job: Ħa mmur. Ser immur.",
          "example": "Se mmur.",
          "gloss": "I am going to go."
        },
        {
          "word": "jekk",
          "means": "if",
          "formed": "jekk does not change. It opens the condition.",
          "example": "Jekk trid.",
          "gloss": "If you want."
        },
        {
          "word": "xi",
          "means": "some, any, what",
          "formed": "xi before a consonant. Before a vowel it is written x': x'inti, x'ismek.",
          "example": "xi ħaġa",
          "gloss": "something"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
